secondaryOutcomes.description:
RILT is defined as clinical radiation pneumonitis and clinical fibrosis. Grading is defined in the protocol as follows (grade 3 and higher):

* Clinical pneumonitis:

  * Grade 3: Severe cough, unresponsive to narcotic antitussive agent and /or dyspnea at rest, with radiographic evidence of acute pneumonitis, and requiring oxygen (intermittent or continuous) for treatment;
  * Grade 4: Radiation pneumonitis causes respiratory insufficiency, requiring assisted ventilation;
  * Grade 5: Radiation pneumonitis directly contributes to the cause of the death;
* Clinical fibrosis:

  * Grade 3: Radiographic evidence of radiation fibrosis causing dyspnea at rest, interfering with activities of daily living, and home oxygen indicated;
  * Grade 4: Radiation fibrosis causes respiratory insufficiency, requiring assisted ventilation;
  * Grade 5: Radiation fibrosis directly contributes to the cause of the death.
